# Walk a character onto a trap he has FOUND and photograph the confirm prompt.
# Read by tools/check_known_trap_prompt.sh, bd inc-o6xj.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/kobold-rogue-seed1.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/known-trap-prompt.keys 3
#
# Move.cpp asks "Confirm move over the <trap>?" before a player steps onto a
# found, armed trap, and now appends "(N% to avoid)" -- or "(cannot be
# avoided)" for a trap with no save. The kobold rogue has Handle Device ranks,
# so OPT_AUTODISARM would disarm the trap before the prompt; that option is 0
# in options-2026-08-22.dat. The trap is created by wizard mode, not reset by
# the character, so the RESET_BY skip does not apply. It is a deathblade scythe
# (level 8, Reflex save, mundane). The answer is "n", so no trap springs.
#
#   Create Trap     a hidden trap one square east.
#   @until "A trap!" s   search until it is found.
#   RIGHT           step onto it; the prompt opens. Photographed, then "n".

w
@while "Enter wizard mode" y
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w
@choose "Create Trap"
"deathblade scythe trap"
ENTER
RIGHT
ENTER
@until "A trap!" s

RIGHT
@dump:prompt
n
@dump:after
